From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 09:35:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bonito: set the FCM target-level to 7

lineage-24.0 ships framework compatibility matrices 7, 8, 202404, 202504,
202604 and 202704 only; AOSP removed level 5 (Android R) and 6 (S) in the
Android 17 finalisation (hardware/interfaces e5b9d41e51, ae70e5eeb9).
libvintf's deprecation check requires a framework matrix at the device's
target-level, so check_vintf_compatible fails with

  Cannot find framework matrix at FCM version 5

Move to 7, the lowest level the tree has. Kernel requirements for level 7
are already not enforced (PRODUCT_OTA_ENFORCE_VINTF_KERNEL_REQUIREMENTS is
false) and the HAL versions bonito serves are all listed in matrix 7.
Same change upstream made for coral/sunfish on lineage-24.0.
---
 manifest.xml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/manifest.xml b/manifest.xml
index 1142dbb6..a0a3869e 100644
--- a/manifest.xml
+++ b/manifest.xml
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-<manifest version="1.0" type="device" target-level="5">
+<manifest version="1.0" type="device" target-level="7">
     <hal format="hidl">
         <name>android.hardware.audio</name>
         <transport>hwbinder</transport>
